Z||000000||fierohoho||05-27-2001||01:38 PM||||I was looking under the dash of my newest project Fiero and noticed that the old owner had been driving it without the clip holding the clutch master cylinder rod to the pedal. It looks to have stayed in place but off center causing the pin to wear half way through.<P>Q: Has anyone replaced just the pedal and not the whole brake/clutch pedal assembly. If so how hard? any tips?<P>Its on a '86 SE 4cyl 5 speed||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||05-27-2001||01:44 PM||||You can replace the clutch pedal itself. I think you can still get the replacement from GM. or maybe it's Fiero Store... I forget...||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||05-27-2001||02:43 PM||||you get the pedal from Gm , if you look around you can find the part #, and just make sure you have a tiny hacksaw cuase that spring thing that wraps around the pedal is a real *****  to get off and it doesn't "bend right off" like some say.. or maybe it was just me <P>John||||reg||1
